The failure is now localized to PID-namespace plumbing: child processes see namespace-local PIDs, while `/proc` exposes different numeric PIDs, and Lean 4.22 resolves its executable through `/proc/<getpid()>/exe`. I’m going to use a narrow audit-only compatibility shim that maps `getpid()` to the outer `NSpid` solely for the Lean/Lake subprocesses, then rerun the unmodified trusted checker and pinned binaries. The shim and its exact source/behavior will be retained as evidence.
